          "comment": "C&D winner who arrives on a hat-trick and could have more left in the tank",
          "spotlight": "C&D 2yo maiden winner; progressive in this 4yo campaign, winning at Salisbury (7f, good to firm) last month and following up at Brighton (7f, good to firm); climbing the weights but could have more left in the tank.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-06-24",
              "horse": "Crimson Spirit",
              "horse_id": "hrs_34473166",
              "race": "Star Sports We Believe In Bookmaking Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11651432",
              "course": "Brighton",
              "course_id": "crs_182",
              "distance_f": "7",
              "distance_y": "1530",
              "quote": "You haven't seen Crimson Spirit at his best there. He went to go and win his race and then got blown around a bit, got unbalanced and the second horse just lunged at him a bit. I thought he did well in difficult circumstances and it was more a case of job done than seeing what he could do - Richard Kingscote, jockey, speaking to Sky Sports Racing."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-08-28",
              "horse": "Crimson Spirit",
              "horse_id": "hrs_34473166",
              "race": "Juddmonte EBF Restricted Maiden Stakes (For Horses In Bands B, C And D) (EBF Qualifier) (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11006073",
              "course": "Epsom",
              "course_id": "crs_442",
              "distance_f": "7",
              "distance_y": "1543",
              "quote": "Crimson Spirit was always in a nice rhythm. He wasn't trying to run to freely early on. He got a nice flow through, found a little gap and picked up nicely. The ground was much nicer than at Nottingham. I was pleased with the way he took me down that hill. We should have some fun with him next year as well - Richard Kingscote, rider."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He ran really well on his reappearance at York. He's a lovely, big, scopey gelding with lots to look forward to as the season progresses. He handles any track, he's versatile and he's a fun horse who should be winning more races. We're looking at Salisbury for him on Sunday. 11-06-25"
            }
          ],
