          "comment": "Has done the majority of his racing abroad; remains to be seen how well treated he is",
          "spotlight": "Has done the majority of his racing abroad, including five wins at Group level at around this trip on the continent; rain wouldn't be a problem on this return to handicap company, but it remains to be seen how well treated he is.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-02-17",
              "horse": "Brave Emperor",
              "horse_id": "hrs_29748698",
              "race": "Irish Thoroughbred Marketing Cup (Local Group 2) (3yo+) (Turf)",
              "race_id": "rac_11192220",
              "course": "Doha",
              "course_id": "crs_31096",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "Everyone adores Brave Emperor, he's a credit to the team and I'm running out of superlatives to describe him. I love the word 'dude', you send him anywhere in the world and he still runs his race - he's such a hero. I thought Cairo was going to come and have a big say, but Luke (Morris, jockey) absolutely nailed that. He's A Monster coming out slightly changed our plan because he was going to be our pace angle, but Luke adapted perfectly. You need a willing partner and there's nobody better than Brave Emperor, who nailed the kick and had it won a long way out - Tim Palin, owner's representative."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-08-06",
              "horse": "Brave Emperor",
              "horse_id": "hrs_29748698",
              "race": "Prix Daphnis - Fonds Europeen de l'Elevage - Prix Famille Saleh-Selman (Group 3)(3yo)(Round)(Turf)",
              "race_id": "rac_11012768",
              "course": "Deauville",
              "course_id": "crs_5356",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "Brave Emperor surprised me. He went into the last two furlongs travelling so strongly and he ground it out lovely to the line when the others came to him. He's a two-time Group 3 winner now and hopefully something a bit better might be ahead. This was his last time to stay in his own age group and we were going to find out how good he is. You'd imagine races like the Daniel Wildenstein on Arc weekend would come into it. I was quite concerned about the soft ground but I felt he improved on today's surface, so it wouldn't bother me going into the autumn on some deep ground - Luke Morris, jockey."
            }
          ],
