          "prev_owners": [
            {
              "owner": "David Ward",
              "owner_id": "own_663128",
              "change_date": "2024-06-13"
            }
          ],
          "comment": "Mainly disappointing since easily winning last year's Buckingham Palace; enough to prove",
          "spotlight": "Highly tried after his impressive win in last year's Buckingham Palace at Royal Ascot (7f, good to firm), but has mainly been disappointing and only beat two home in the same race four weeks ago; rain not a problem but still has enough to prove; cheekpieces removed after one use.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-06-20",
              "horse": "English Oak",
              "horse_id": "hrs_35269703",
              "race": "Buckingham Palace Stakes (Handicap)",
              "race_id": "rac_11299483",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "7",
              "distance_y": "1540",
              "quote": "English Oak is clearly a classy sort, he travelled superbly through the race. We had a massive advantage on the stands' side, even after going a furlong or so we were a long way ahead of the others. He's very speedy. He's got a high cruising speed, he does feel pretty fast. When I let him go there he quickened up pretty smartly. It will be interesting to see what the guys want to do - James Doyle, rider."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-07-05",
              "horse": "English Oak",
              "horse_id": "hrs_35269703",
              "race": "British EBF Novice Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_10959741",
              "course": "Thirsk",
              "course_id": "crs_2080",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1758",
              "quote": "He's a slow-maturing horse who was like a rabbit in the headlights first time. English Oak has seen the trip out really well and is definitely one to keep on the right side - P J McDonald, jockey."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He's been disappointing since winning at the meeting 12 months ago. He needs to spark back into life, but he's started to come back down to the mark he won off last year [1lb higher now], so it's not impossible. He looks well and we gave him a bit of time after his last race. 10-06-25"
            },
            {
              "quote": "He was a bit disappointing after putting up such a good performance when winning the Buckingham Palace at Royal Ascot, so we hope we can get him back on track this year. He's been gelded and I hope that will help him. He's a bit behind and is taking a long time to come in his coat, so we're not in a rush with him. He'll probably start back in a conditions or Listed race. I think he's best at that specialist trip of 7f but we'll see how we go. 16-04-25"
            }
          ],
