          "owner": "Sheikh Ahmed Al Maktoum",
          "owner_id": "own_59124",
          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "2-3; open to plenty more progress now handicapping; holds a Great Voltigeur entry",
          "spotlight": "Beautifully bred and didn't need to improve much on previous form to land a five-runner novice over C&D (good to firm; 1-3) in May (held Group 1 entries at the time); subsequent wins by the second and third give the form some substance and he remains open to plenty more progress now handicapping; debut win came on soft; still holds a Great Voltigeur entry.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-05-04",
              "horse": "Sallaal",
              "horse_id": "hrs_45701796",
              "race": "Darley Stallions EBF Novice Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11591489",
              "course": "Hamilton",
              "course_id": "crs_572",
              "distance_f": "8.5",
              "distance_y": "1828",
              "quote": "Sallaal ticks all the boxes. He's very well related to a lot of nice horses, he's a Frankel and that's in him as he's a little bit quirky sometimes, but he's still a big baby and we brought him here hoping he'd race properly and relax, and he did. He realised what his job was in the last furlong. I felt Arctic Grey come to me and we both got racing together down the hill. When I gave him a reminder he really put his head down and galloped strongly through the line, which is what we were all expecting and hoping he'd do - Ray Dawson, jockey."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-10-15",
              "horse": "Sallaal",
              "horse_id": "hrs_45701796",
              "race": "British Stallion Studs EBF Novice Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11398426",
              "course": "Yarmouth",
              "course_id": "crs_2704",
              "distance_f": "7",
              "distance_y": "1543",
              "quote": "Sallaal has been a true professional. The only time he wasn't was when they quickened and he couldn't find his legs, but he dealt with it quite well. He showed a bit of class - Jack Mitchell, rider."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "There's a lot to like about him. He took all last year to strengthen and wasn't the finished article by a long way when he went to Yarmouth, so I was delighted that he won. He carries all the big entries and is a half-brother to Elmalka and Benbatl, so he's got a bit to live up to. Time will tell if he can match their ability but I think he's quite smart. He's almost ready to run and his first run will tell us a whole lot more. 11-04-25"
            }
          ],
