          "comment": "Guineas' flops now on a reputation-restoring mission; rain would suit",
          "spotlight": "Mighty run in the Group 1 Dewhurst (7f, soft) at Newmarket last year when beaten only a neck by Shadow Of Light but very disappointing in both Guineas' in the spring, fading after showing up for much of way at Newmarket and then never counting after a slow start at the Curragh; on a reputation-restoring mission here and don't rule a bounce back to form, especially if the ground eases.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-10-12",
              "horse": "Expanded",
              "horse_id": "hrs_41325193",
              "race": "Darley Dewhurst Stakes (Group 1) (No Geldings)",
              "race_id": "rac_11350014",
              "course": "Newmarket",
              "course_id": "crs_988",
              "distance_f": "7",
              "distance_y": "1540",
              "quote": "Expanded has run a great race considering we only ran him at the Curragh seven days ago but Ryan said that if James Doyle hadn't attacked him early on Ancient Truth he would have won. He was here for experience more than anything, to run against The Lion In Winter originally, but we've always liked him and he went to the Curragh on the back of five pieces of work. As we know he handles the track, he could be back here next year - Aidan O'Brien, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-10-05",
              "horse": "Expanded",
              "horse_id": "hrs_41325193",
              "race": "Irish Stallion Farms EBF (C & G) Maiden",
              "race_id": "rac_11418901",
              "course": "Curragh",
              "course_id": "crs_4628",
              "distance_f": "7",
              "distance_y": "1540",
              "quote": "Expanded is a lovely horse with loads of class but still very raw. When he puts everything together he is going to be a smashing colt - Chris Armstrong, assistant trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He got beat a short head in the Dewhurst having got kind of a raw deal. He was going into the race for experience mainly as second string behind The Lion In Winter, but that horse didn't run and he got put into the front line, so it was a massive run on his second start. He's being trained for Guineas weekend but he could go to the Curragh for the Tetrarch the day after the Guineas if he doesn't go to Newmarket. If Twain goes to Newmarket, he might take the easier option at the Curragh, given he's not a Group winner. 07-04-25"
            }
          ],
