          "comment": "Ascot also-ran; remains open to improvement and this drop in class should suit",
          "spotlight": "Sister to high-class miler Dancing Gemini came good in 1m maiden at Gowran (good) last month but unable to land a blow in this headgear combination in very competitive Sandringham Stakes at Ascot, not disgraced in midfield; remains open to improvement and this drop in class should suit.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-06-02",
              "horse": "Dancing Teapot",
              "horse_id": "hrs_46850734",
              "race": "Today's Gate Sponsored By The INPBA Fillies Maiden",
              "race_id": "rac_11659492",
              "course": "Gowran Park",
              "course_id": "crs_4784",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "The draw can be a bit of a killer here as position is so important but Dancing Teapot did well to get across. I think she's a filly who can progress. She's still rated low but hopefully she can go up through the ranks. Dylan [Browne McMonagle, jockey] felt she was waiting a bit in front but she galloped to the line. She's a very good worker and has a very good pedigree. Her brother looks like a miler but she might stay a bit further - Joseph O'Brien, trainer."
            }
          ],
